Ours.  The ZZ9000/Z3660 screen is built on X's own 16-bit framebuffer code
(cfb16ScreenInit) instead of the hand-built screen, GC and drawing layer.

- cfb16 owns visuals, windows, pixmaps (mfb for depth 1), GCs and their
  validation, all drawing, colormaps and text: planemask, dashed and wide
  lines, pixmap drawing and depth-1 pixmaps are cfb's;
- TrueColor only at depth 16, the visual set to the card's RGB565 (cfb's
  depth-16 default is 6-5-5 with red low);
- the card's blitter at four points: window-to-window CopyArea through
  cfb's own BitBlt (clipping, exposures) with a blitter doBitBlt,
  CopyWindow, solid GXcopy PolyFillRect, solid PaintWindow; each flushes
  the queue before returning, so cfb's CPU drawing never meets a pending
  blit.  PutImage of a 16-bit picture into a window keeps the direct path;
- zz9000win.c, zz9000cmap.c, zz9000pix.c and zz9000cursor.c go, and so does
  the rtg layer's own GC private and visual.

